      "widgets_values": [
        "integrated_multimodal_description: [Shot 1] Live-action, mockumentary, a medium-wide static shot frames a dull open-plan office under flat fluorescent light \u2014 desks with monitors, sticky notes, a large window with closed blinds in the background. A young man in his late 20s with tousled brown hair, wearing a light blue button-down shirt and loosened dark tie (S1), stands in the aisle holding up a white ceramic mug reading \"World's Most Mediocre Boss\" toward the camera with both hands, looking straight into the lens with forced confidence. The camera holds a static shot. The young man with an earnest, slightly nasal voice at a quick, nervous rate (S1) says: <d>[English] You know what? I've decided to aim higher.</d>\n[Shot 2] At 00:03.000, the camera pushes in with small amplitude at slow speed toward him as he sneers at the window, winds up with his right arm, and hurls the mug reading \"World's Most Mediocre Boss\" toward the office window. The young man (S1) says: <d>[English] Watch this.</d>\n[Shot 3] At 00:05.800, the camera holds a static shot as the mug hits the reinforced window glass with a dull clunk, fails to break it, and bounces straight back in a slow arc toward him, spinning in the air.\n[Shot 4] At 00:07.200, the camera tilts down at slow speed as the mug smacks him squarely in the forehead, he keeps a perfectly deadpan, eyes-wide expression for a beat, then falls stiff as a plank straight backwards onto the thin office carpet with his arms pinned at his sides, the mug clattering beside him while two coworkers in the background freeze and stare.\n\noverall_soundscape: Low office ambience with faint keyboard clatter, air conditioning hum, and distant phones. A sharp whoosh as the mug is thrown, a dull clunk on the window glass, a second sharper thwack as it hits his forehead, then a soft thud as he hits the carpet followed by the mug clattering and stifled gasps and short, shocked laughter from coworkers.\n\nnon_diegetic_music: N/A",
        960,
        544,
        241
      ],
      "widgets_values_named": {
        "prompt": "integrated_multimodal_description: [Shot 1] Live-action, mockumentary, a medium-wide static shot frames a dull open-plan office under flat fluorescent light \u2014 desks with monitors, sticky notes, a large window with closed blinds in the background. A young man in his late 20s with tousled brown hair, wearing a light blue button-down shirt and loosened dark tie (S1), stands in the aisle holding up a white ceramic mug reading \"World's Most Mediocre Boss\" toward the camera with both hands, looking straight into the lens with forced confidence. The camera holds a static shot. The young man with an earnest, slightly nasal voice at a quick, nervous rate (S1) says: <d>[English] You know what? I've decided to aim higher.</d>\n[Shot 2] At 00:03.000, the camera pushes in with small amplitude at slow speed toward him as he sneers at the window, winds up with his right arm, and hurls the mug reading \"World's Most Mediocre Boss\" toward the office window. The young man (S1) says: <d>[English] Watch this.</d>\n[Shot 3] At 00:05.800, the camera holds a static shot as the mug hits the reinforced window glass with a dull clunk, fails to break it, and bounces straight back in a slow arc toward him, spinning in the air.\n[Shot 4] At 00:07.200, the camera tilts down at slow speed as the mug smacks him squarely in the forehead, he keeps a perfectly deadpan, eyes-wide expression for a beat, then falls stiff as a plank straight backwards onto the thin office carpet with his arms pinned at his sides, the mug clattering beside him while two coworkers in the background freeze and stare.\n\noverall_soundscape: Low office ambience with faint keyboard clatter, air conditioning hum, and distant phones. A sharp whoosh as the mug is thrown, a dull clunk on the window glass, a second sharper thwack as it hits his forehead, then a soft thud as he hits the carpet followed by the mug clattering and stifled gasps and short, shocked laughter from coworkers.\n\nnon_diegetic_music: N/A",
