    {
      "id": 30,
      "type": "MarkdownNote",
      "pos": [
        -520,
        30
      ],
      "size": [
        460,
        1322
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 24,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "title": "Note: MiniMax H3 SPEED",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "## MiniMax H3\n\n[MiniMax H3](https://www.minimax.io/blog/minimax-h3) generates video with native stereo audio (voice, effects and music) in one pass. Models: see the Model Links note.\n\n- **Prompt**: the shots, camera moves and the audio in one block.\n- **Resolution Selector**: width and height. H3's native canvas is a 768 px short edge, rounded to a multiple of 32; sizes are in the size note.\n- **Duration (seconds)**: the Length node snaps it up to H3's 17k+5 frame grid at 24 fps.\n\nRTX 5080, this 10 s clip at 960x544: native 571 s, Automatic (3 stages, \u0394 0.005) 439 s (1.30x), \u0394 0.01 410 s (1.39x). Full table and GIFs: evidence/h3_evidence.\n\n## SPEED on H3\n\nAll SPEED nodes here have **model_type = h3_video** and **noise_policy = direct_coarse**. The sampler input comes from KSamplerSelect (euler). Audio always stays at full resolution.\n\n1. **Harvest** (muted): unmute it, run once, and read the report. Paste `noise_amplitude` and\n   `noise_decay_exponent` into the Automatic node. Only needed when you change the model, LoRA,\n   sampler or sigma schedule: Automatic already has the baked H3 Euler calibration.\n2. **SPEED Automatic** (active): stage boundaries come from the calibration and `Tolerance (Delta)`.\n   \u0394 0.005 is conservative; \u0394 0.01 is faster at near parity; \u0394 0.05 shows artifacts on video.\n3. **SPEED Manual** (muted): fixed boundaries, 0.25x to step 3, 0.5x to step 5, then full resolution.\n   Unmute it and mute Automatic to use it instead.\n"
      ],
      "widgets_values_named": {
        "text": "## MiniMax H3\n\n[MiniMax H3](https://www.minimax.io/blog/minimax-h3) generates video with native stereo audio (voice, effects and music) in one pass. Models: see the Model Links note.\n\n- **Prompt**: the shots, camera moves and the audio in one block.\n- **Resolution Selector**: width and height. H3's native canvas is a 768 px short edge, rounded to a multiple of 32; sizes are in the size note.\n- **Duration (seconds)**: the Length node snaps it up to H3's 17k+5 frame grid at 24 fps.\n\nRTX 5080, this 10 s clip at 960x544: native 571 s, Automatic (3 stages, \u0394 0.005) 439 s (1.30x), \u0394 0.01 410 s (1.39x). Full table and GIFs: evidence/h3_evidence.\n\n## SPEED on H3\n\nAll SPEED nodes here have **model_type = h3_video** and **noise_policy = direct_coarse**. The sampler input comes from KSamplerSelect (euler). Audio always stays at full resolution.\n\n1. **Harvest** (muted): unmute it, run once, and read the report. Paste `noise_amplitude` and\n   `noise_decay_exponent` into the Automatic node. Only needed when you change the model, LoRA,\n   sampler or sigma schedule: Automatic already has the baked H3 Euler calibration.\n2. **SPEED Automatic** (active): stage boundaries come from the calibration and `Tolerance (Delta)`.\n   \u0394 0.005 is conservative; \u0394 0.01 is faster at near parity; \u0394 0.05 shows artifacts on video.\n3. **SPEED Manual** (muted): fixed boundaries, 0.25x to step 3, 0.5x to step 5, then full resolution.\n   Unmute it and mute Automatic to use it instead.\n"
      },
      "color": "#222",
      "bgcolor": "#000"
    },
